# GitHub delivery

Deliver work in small, buildable chunks. Prefer a linear sequence of short-lived branches over one long modernization branch.

## Commits

- One purpose per commit: deps, refactor, fix, tests, docs, or generated files — not mixed
- Include the regression test with the fix (or a preceding test-only commit that fails first)
- Keep each commit buildable on Windows

## Pull requests

- One independently reviewable outcome per PR
- Link issue, acceptance gate, tests, and migration impact
- Rebase onto the merged predecessor so the PR shows only its own delta

## Preferred sequence

1. Build metadata / toolchain
2. CI skeleton
3. Pure test seams
4. Settings schema + fixtures
5. Electron smoke harness
6. Correctness fixes (one area per PR)
7. Renderer injection hardening
8. IPC hardening by capability group
9. Editor module extraction
10. Runtime reliability (hotkeys, modes, DPI, etc.)
11. AHK v2 subsystem ports
